/* Invalid: P x holds exactly when x > 150 (every k >= x must differ from
   150), so x = 121 is a counterexample.  The counterexamples are exactly
   121..150, all beyond 100, so a dual problem whose existential (the negated
   universal) is searched for in [-100, 100] only is refutable although the
   dual itself is valid: that refutation must not be flipped into valid. */
forall (x: int). x <= 120 \/ P x
s.t.
P (x: int): bool =nu x != 150 /\ P (x + 1);
